/** The Neovim plugin's files, by path relative to the plugin root. */
export const NVIM_PLUGIN_FILES: Record<string, string> = {
  "README.md": "# hedgesync.nvim\n\nLive-edit HedgeDoc notes in Neovim, keystroke by keystroke, together with\npeople in the browser. Their edits appear in your buffer as they type, and\ntheir cursors are shown inline with their names.\n\nRequires Neovim 0.11+ and the `hedgesync` CLI.\n\n## Install\n\nThe plugin ships inside the `hedgesync` binary, so the two always match:\n\n```sh\n# 1. The CLI: a release binary (or `npm i -g hedgesync`)\ncurl -fL https://github.com/tionis/hedgesync/releases/latest/download/hedgesync-linux-x64 \\\n  -o ~/.local/bin/hedgesync && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/hedgesync\n\n# 2. The plugin, into Neovim's package directory\nhedgesync editor nvim install\n\n# 3. A login (the plugin uses the CLI's saved sessions)\nhedgesync login https://md.example.com --from-browser firefox --save   # or -u <user>\n```\n\nThen check everything with `:checkhealth hedgesync`. After updating the CLI,\nrun `hedgesync editor nvim install` again (`hedgesync editor nvim status`\ntells you whether you need to). Local edits to the installed plugin are never\noverwritten without `--force`. If the CLI and the plugin speak different\nprotocol versions, the plugin refuses to start and tells you which to update.\n\nNeovim loads the package directory by itself. lazy.nvim does not, so add a\nspec pointing at it (`install` prints it):\n\n```lua\n{\n  dir = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/pack/hedgesync/start/hedgesync.nvim\",\n  name = \"hedgesync.nvim\",\n  cond = vim.uv.fs_stat(vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/site/pack/hedgesync/start/hedgesync.nvim\") ~= nil,\n  lazy = false,\n  opts = {},\n}\n```\n\nDon't lazy-load it on `BufReadCmd`: lazy.nvim then loads the plugin but does\nnot replay the `:e hedgedoc://...` that triggered it. Loading it eagerly costs\nnothing, because the startup file only defines `:Hedge` and an autocmd; the\nmodule loads on first use.\n\nTo hack on the plugin, point `dir` at `editors/nvim` in a checkout instead\nand run the CLI from the same checkout (`cmd = { \"bun\", \"<checkout>/bin/hedgesync.ts\" }`).\n\n## Use\n\nFrom the shell, `hedgesync edit <url>` starts Neovim on the note, and\n`hedgesync edit` alone opens your notes to pick from (both work even before\nthe plugin is installed: they load the matching copy for that session).\nInside Neovim:\n\n```vim\n:Hedge open https://md.example.com/abc123\n:e hedgedoc://md.example.com/abc123       \" same thing; also `nvim hedgedoc://... +42`\n:Hedge browse [server]                     \" your notes (see below)\n:Hedge find [server]                       \" pick a note with vim.ui.select / your fuzzy finder\n:Hedge new [title]                         \" create a note and open it\n:'<,'>Hedge new                            \" ... with the selected lines as its content\n:Hedge search <text>                       \" search your notes' text into the quickfix list\n:Hedge revisions                           \" this note's revisions: view, diff, restore\n:Hedge url [publish|slide]                 \" copy the note's (published, slide) URL\n:Hedge share [permission]                  \" share this file buffer live (see below)\n:Hedge follow [name]                       \" your view follows their cursor\n:Hedge users                               \" who else is in the note\n:Hedge status\n:Hedge close                               \" stop syncing this buffer\n```\n\n`:Hedge browse` lists the notes in your HedgeDoc history, pinned first,\nwith tags and when you last opened them. The server is the one given, the\ncurrent note's, the last one used, or your saved login's (you are asked if\nthere are several). Keys (`?` shows them):\n\n| Key | | Key | |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `<CR>` | open | `<C-v>` / `<C-x>` | open in a vertical / horizontal split |\n| `n` | new note | `p` | pin / unpin |\n| `r` | revisions | `y` | copy the URL |\n| `D` | remove from history (the note stays) | `s` | search text (quickfix) |\n| `R` | reload | `q` | close |\n\nIn `:Hedge revisions`, `<CR>` shows a revision, `d` diffs it against the\nlive note side by side, and `R` restores it. Restoring is an edit in the\nlive buffer, synced like typing, so `u` takes it back.\n\n`:Hedge share` shares the file you are editing, code or anything else: a\nnew note gets its text, and the buffer stays your file (`:w` saves it, as\nalways) while it syncs with the note. The link it copies (`:Hedge url` shows\nit again) opens the editor view in a browser; in Neovim, `:Hedge open\n<link>` takes the filetype from it, and `hedgesync share <file> <link>`\njoins from any other editor. `:Hedge close` stops sharing.\n\n`:Hedge follow` keeps your cursor on someone else's, scrolling along, for\npairing or a walkthrough. While you follow, your own cursor is hidden from\nthe others. Any key stops it (`:` commands do not), as does `:Hedge follow`\nagain; the statusline helper shows `following <name>`.\n\nSearch results open the note live at the matching line (`:cnext` and\nfriends work as usual). Notes appear in your history once opened while\nsigned in, which includes opening them with this plugin.\n\nThere is nothing to save: every change is sent as you make it, and `:w`\njust confirms the connection state. If the connection drops, keep typing;\nyour edits are sent once the bridge reconnects.\n\nFor a statusline: `require(\"hedgesync\").status()` returns e.g.\n`● connected`, and `b:hedgesync_title` holds the note title.\n\n## Options\n\n```lua\nrequire(\"hedgesync\").setup({\n  cmd = { \"hedgesync\" },   -- how to run the CLI, e.g. { \"bun\", \"/path/to/bin/hedgesync.ts\" }\n  args = {},               -- extra args for `hedgesync bridge`, e.g. { \"--cookie\", \"...\" }\n  cursors = true,          -- show other people's cursors\n  cursor_debounce = 50,    -- ms before sending your cursor position\n})\n```\n\n## How it works\n\nEach note buffer starts `hedgesync bridge <url>`, which holds the HedgeDoc\nconnection and exchanges newline-delimited JSON with the plugin. Because the\neditor and the bridge are separate processes, a remote edit can be in flight\nwhile you type; the bridge runs a second OT link toward the editor (all\ntransforming happens in the bridge; the plugin applies a remote edit only if\nit has typed nothing since, and the bridge resends dropped ones rebased). The\nprotocol is documented in `src/editor-bridge.ts`.\n\nThe plugin does not trust `on_bytes` for content: some commands (`J`, undo)\nreport changes before the buffer holds the new text. It keeps a snapshot of\nthe lines and diffs it against the buffer after each command instead. Every\nchange carries the buffer size, so if the two sides ever disagree the buffer\nis reset from the note rather than drifting.\n\n`HEDGESYNC_BRIDGE_LOG=/tmp/bridge.log nvim` traces the protocol.\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- `u` undoes other people's edits too when they are interleaved with yours:\n  Neovim has one undo history per buffer and cannot skip remote changes.\n- A note is shown with lines joined by `\\n`; `\\r\\n` line endings from\n  Windows clients show as `^M`.\n- HedgeDoc 1 has no \"all my notes\" listing: browse and search see the notes\n  in your history (`hedgesync export` gets everything you own).\n",
  "lua/hedgesync/health.lua": "-- :checkhealth hedgesync\nlocal M = {}\n\nlocal function run(cmd, args)\n  local ok, proc = pcall(vim.system, vim.list_extend(vim.deepcopy(cmd), args), { text = true })\n  if not ok then\n    return nil, tostring(proc)\n  end\n  local result = proc:wait(15000)\n  if result.code ~= 0 then\n    return nil, vim.trim((result.stderr or \"\") .. (result.stdout or \"\"))\n  end\n  return result.stdout\nend\n\nfunction M.check()\n  local h = vim.health\n  local hs = require(\"hedgesync\")\n  local cmd = hs.config.cmd\n\n  h.start(\"hedgesync.nvim\")\n  if vim.fn.has(\"nvim-0.11\") == 1 then\n    h.ok(\"Neovim \" .. tostring(vim.version()))\n  else\n    h.error(\"Neovim 0.11 or newer is required, this is \" .. tostring(vim.version()))\n  end\n\n  if vim.fn.executable(cmd[1]) ~= 1 then\n    h.error((\"`%s` is not on PATH\"):format(cmd[1]), {\n      \"Install the hedgesync CLI from https://github.com/tionis/hedgesync/releases (or `npm i -g hedgesync`)\",\n      \"or point `cmd` in require('hedgesync').setup() at it\",\n    })\n    return\n  end\n\n  local out, err = run(cmd, { \"bridge\", \"--info\" })\n  local info = out and pcall(vim.json.decode, out) and vim.json.decode(out) or nil\n  if not info then\n    h.error(\"`\" .. table.concat(cmd, \" \") .. \"` has no editor bridge (too old?)\", { \"Update the hedgesync CLI\", err })\n    return\n  end\n  if info.protocol == hs.protocol then\n    h.ok((\"hedgesync %s (%s), editor protocol %d\"):format(info.version, vim.fn.exepath(cmd[1]), info.protocol))\n  else\n    h.error(hs._protocol_problem(info.protocol, info.version))\n  end\n\n  -- The CLI compares the installed files with the copy it bundles. `status`\n  -- exits 1 unless they match, so read its JSON whatever the exit code.\n  local ran, proc = pcall(vim.system, vim.list_extend(vim.deepcopy(cmd), { \"editor\", \"nvim\", \"status\", \"--json\", \"--dir\", hs.root }), { text = true })\n  local ok_status, status = false, nil\n  if ran then\n    ok_status, status = pcall(vim.json.decode, proc:wait(15000).stdout or \"\")\n  end\n  if not ok_status or type(status) ~= \"table\" then\n    h.warn(\"Could not check the plugin install (`hedgesync editor nvim status` failed)\")\n  elseif status.state == \"unmanaged\" then\n    h.info(\"Plugin loaded from \" .. hs.root .. \" (not installed by `hedgesync editor nvim install`)\")\n  elseif status.state == \"current\" then\n    h.ok(\"Plugin in \" .. hs.root .. \" matches the CLI\")\n  elseif #(status.edited or {}) > 0 or #(status.missing or {}) > 0 then\n    h.warn(\n      \"Plugin in \" .. hs.root .. \" has local changes: \" .. table.concat(vim.list_extend(status.edited or {}, status.missing or {}), \", \"),\n      { \"`hedgesync editor nvim install --force` restores the bundled copy\" }\n    )\n  else\n    h.warn(\n      (\"Plugin was installed by hedgesync %s and differs from the copy in the CLI (%s)\"):format(\n        tostring(status.version),\n        info.version\n      ),\n      { \"Run `hedgesync editor nvim install` to update it\" }\n    )\n  end\n\n  h.start(\"hedgesync logins\")\n  local sessions_out = run(cmd, { \"sessions\", \"--json\" })\n  local ok, data = pcall(vim.json.decode, sessions_out or \"\")\n  local sessions = ok and type(data) == \"table\" and data.sessions or nil\n  if sessions == nil then\n    h.warn(\"Could not list saved logins (`hedgesync sessions --json` failed)\")\n  elseif #sessions == 0 then\n    h.warn(\"No saved logins; notes that need an account will be read-only or refused\", {\n      \"Run `hedgesync login <server> --from-browser firefox --save` (or `-u <user>` for email/LDAP)\",\n    })\n  else\n    for _, s in ipairs(sessions) do\n      local who = type(s.user) == \"table\" and s.user.name or s.user\n      h.ok((\"%s%s\"):format(s.server, who and (\" as \" .. tostring(who)) or \"\"))\n    end\n  end\n\n  h.start(\"hedgesync sessions in this Neovim\")\n  local any = false\n  for _, buf in ipairs(vim.api.nvim_list_bufs()) do\n    local s = hs.session(buf)\n    if s then\n      any = true\n      h.info((\"%s: %s\"):format(s.url, hs.status(buf)))\n    end\n  end\n  if not any then\n    h.info(\"No notes open\")\n  end\nend\n\nreturn M\n",
  "lua/hedgesync/init.lua": "-- hedgesync.nvim: live-edit HedgeDoc notes, keystroke by keystroke.\n--\n-- Each note buffer runs `hedgesync bridge <url>` and exchanges JSON lines with\n-- it. The bridge does all operational transformation; this side only reports\n-- buffer changes and applies remote edits whose `base` matches the\n-- number of changes it has sent, dropping stale ones (the bridge resends them\n-- rebased). See src/editor-bridge.ts for the protocol.\n\nlocal M = {}\n\n--- Editor protocol this plugin speaks (BRIDGE_PROTOCOL in src/editor-bridge.ts).\nM.protocol = 1\n\n--- Plugin root directory (holds .hedgesync-install.json when installed by\n--- `hedgesync editor nvim install`).\nM.root = vim.fn.fnamemodify(debug.getinfo(1, \"S\").source:sub(2), \":p:h:h:h\")\n\n--- The CLI to run: $HEDGESYNC_CMD (a JSON list, set by `hedgesync edit` so the\n--- bridge is the binary that started Neovim), else hedgesync on PATH.\nlocal function default_cmd()\n  local ok, cmd = pcall(vim.json.decode, vim.env.HEDGESYNC_CMD or \"\")\n  if ok and type(cmd) == \"table\" and type(cmd[1]) == \"string\" then\n    return cmd\n  end\n  return { \"hedgesync\" }\nend\n\nM.config = {\n  -- Command that runs the hedgesync CLI.\n  cmd = default_cmd(),\n  -- Extra arguments for `hedgesync bridge` (e.g. { \"--cookie\", \"...\" }).\n  args = {},\n  -- Show other people's cursors.\n  cursors = true,\n  -- Delay before sending cursor moves (ms).\n  cursor_debounce = 50,\n}\n\nlocal api = vim.api\nlocal ns = api.nvim_create_namespace(\"hedgesync_cursors\")\n---@type table<integer, table>\nlocal sessions = {}\n\nlocal function notify(msg, level)\n  vim.notify(\"hedgesync: \" .. msg, level or vim.log.levels.INFO)\nend\n\nlocal function send(s, msg)\n  if s.closed or not s.proc then\n    return\n  end\n  local ok, err = pcall(function()\n    s.proc:write(vim.json.encode(msg) .. \"\\n\")\n  end)\n  if not ok then\n    s.closed = true\n    notify(\"bridge is gone: \" .. tostring(err), vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n  end\nend\n\nlocal function buf_size(buf)\n  return api.nvim_buf_get_offset(buf, api.nvim_buf_line_count(buf))\nend\n\nlocal function is_cont(str, i)\n  local b = str:byte(i)\n  return b ~= nil and b >= 0x80 and b < 0xC0\nend\n\n--- Row and byte column of byte offset `off` in `text`.\nlocal function rowcol(text, off)\n  local row, start = 0, 1\n  while true do\n    local nl = text:find(\"\\n\", start, true)\n    if not nl or nl > off then\n      break\n    end\n    row, start = row + 1, nl + 1\n  end\n  return row, off - (start - 1)\nend\n\n--- Report what changed since the last snapshot as one change message.\n---\n--- on_bytes only marks the buffer dirty: for some commands (J, for one) it\n--- fires before the buffer holds the new text, so the text is read here, once\n--- the command is done, by diffing against a snapshot of the lines. Lua\n--- interns strings, so unchanged lines compare in O(1).\nlocal function flush(s)\n  if not s.dirty then\n    return\n  end\n  s.dirty = false\n  local buf = s.buf\n  if s.closed or not api.nvim_buf_is_valid(buf) then\n    return\n  end\n  local old = s.lines\n  local new = api.nvim_buf_get_lines(buf, 0, -1, false)\n  local n_old, n_new = #old, #new\n  -- Compare from the top: on_bytes rows are not trustworthy either (undo).\n  local i = 0 -- 0-based first changed line\n  while i < n_old and i < n_new and old[i + 1] == new[i + 1] do\n    i = i + 1\n  end\n  local k = 0 -- unchanged lines at the end\n  while k < n_old - i and k < n_new - i and old[n_old - k] == new[n_new - k] do\n    k = k + 1\n  end\n  s.lines = new\n  if i == n_old - k and i == n_new - k then\n    return -- changed and changed back\n  end\n  -- The changed blocks, every line ending in \"\\n\" (the on_bytes model).\n  local o = table.concat(old, \"\\n\", i + 1, n_old - k) .. (n_old - k > i and \"\\n\" or \"\")\n  local n = table.concat(new, \"\\n\", i + 1, n_new - k) .. (n_new - k > i and \"\\n\" or \"\")\n  -- Narrow to the changed bytes, on UTF-8 character boundaries.\n  local p, max = 0, math.min(#o, #n)\n  while p < max and o:byte(p + 1) == n:byte(p + 1) do\n    p = p + 1\n  end\n  while p > 0 and (is_cont(o, p + 1) or is_cont(n, p + 1)) do\n    p = p - 1\n  end\n  local q = 0\n  while q < max - p and o:byte(#o - q) == n:byte(#n - q) do\n    q = q + 1\n  end\n  while q > 0 and is_cont(o, #o - q + 1) do\n    q = q - 1\n  end\n  local srow, scol = rowcol(o, p)\n  local erow, ecol = rowcol(o, #o - q)\n  s.E = s.E + 1\n  send(s, {\n    t = \"change\",\n    epoch = s.epoch,\n    seen = s.R,\n    sr = i + srow,\n    sc = scol,\n    oer = erow - srow,\n    oec = erow == srow and ecol - scol or ecol,\n    text = n:sub(p + 1, #n - q),\n    size = buf_size(buf),\n  })\n  vim.bo[buf].modified = false\nend\n\n--- Apply text without reporting it back to the bridge.\nlocal function apply(s, fn)\n  local buf = s.buf\n  local modifiable, readonly = vim.bo[buf].modifiable, vim.bo[buf].readonly\n  s.applying = true\n  -- Lift both, or Neovim warns \"W10: Changing a readonly file\" about our own write.\n  vim.bo[buf].modifiable, vim.bo[buf].readonly = true, false\n  local ok, err = pcall(fn)\n  vim.bo[buf].modifiable, vim.bo[buf].readonly = modifiable, readonly\n  s.applying = false\n  vim.bo[buf].modified = false\n  s.lines = api.nvim_buf_get_lines(buf, 0, -1, false)\n  return ok, err\nend\n\nlocal function set_modifiable(s)\n  vim.bo[s.buf].modifiable = s.editable and not s.closed\n  vim.bo[s.buf].readonly = not s.editable\nend\n\nlocal function update_status(s, state)\n  s.state = state\n  vim.b[s.buf].hedgesync_state = state\n  vim.cmd.redrawstatus()\nend\n\n-- Remote cursors -----------------------------------------------------------\n\nlocal hl_cache = {}\n\n--- \"#rgb\" / \"#rrggbb\" (HedgeDoc sends both) as \"#rrggbb\", or nil.\nlocal function normalize_color(color)\n  local hex = type(color) == \"string\" and color:match(\"^#?(%x+)$\")\n  if hex and #hex == 3 then\n    hex = hex:gsub(\".\", \"%0%0\")\n  end\n  return hex and #hex == 6 and (\"#\" .. hex:lower()) or nil\nend\n\nlocal function cursor_hl(color)\n  color = normalize_color(color) or \"#888888\"\n  local name = \"HedgesyncCursor_\" .. color:sub(2)\n  if not hl_cache[name] then\n    local r, g, b = tonumber(color:sub(2, 3), 16), tonumber(color:sub(4, 5), 16), tonumber(color:sub(6, 7), 16)\n    local fg = (0.299 * r + 0.587 * g + 0.114 * b) > 140 and \"#000000\" or \"#ffffff\"\n    api.nvim_set_hl(0, name, { bg = color, fg = fg })\n    api.nvim_set_hl(0, name .. \"Label\", { fg = color, italic = true })\n    hl_cache[name] = true\n  end\n  return name\nend\n\nlocal function draw_cursors(s, cursors)\n  local buf = s.buf\n  api.nvim_buf_clear_namespace(buf, ns, 0, -1)\n  if not M.config.cursors then\n    return\n  end\n  local line_count = api.nvim_buf_line_count(buf)\n  for _, c in ipairs(cursors) do\n    if c.row and c.row < line_count then\n      local line = api.nvim_buf_get_lines(buf, c.row, c.row + 1, false)[1] or \"\"\n      local col = math.min(c.col, #line)\n      local hl = cursor_hl(c.color or \"#888888\")\n      local opts = {\n        virt_text = { { \" \" .. c.name, hl .. \"Label\" } },\n        virt_text_pos = \"eol\",\n        priority = 200,\n      }\n      if col < #line then\n        -- Highlight the character under the cursor (one UTF-8 character).\n        local char_end = vim.str_byteindex(line, \"utf-32\", vim.str_utfindex(line, \"utf-32\", col) + 1, false)\n        opts.end_col = char_end\n        opts.hl_group = hl\n      else\n        opts.virt_text = { { \" \", hl }, { \" \" .. c.name, hl .. \"Label\" } }\n        opts.virt_text_pos = \"overlay\"\n      end\n      pcall(api.nvim_buf_set_extmark, buf, ns, c.row, col, opts)\n    end\n  end\nend\n\n-- Messages from the bridge -------------------------------------------------\n\n-- Follow mode ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nlocal follow_ns = api.nvim_create_namespace(\"hedgesync_follow\")\n\nlocal function stop_following(s, why)\n  if not s.follow then\n    return\n  end\n  local name = s.follow.name\n  s.follow = nil\n  vim.on_key(nil, follow_ns)\n  if why then\n    notify((\"stopped following %s (%s)\"):format(name, why))\n  end\n  if api.nvim_get_current_buf() == s.buf and s.send_cursor then\n    s.send_cursor() -- visible again\n  end\nend\n\n--- Move to the followed person's cursor (current window only), centring it\n--- when it left the screen.\nlocal function follow_update(s)\n  local f = s.follow\n  if not f then\n    return\n  end\n  local who\n  for _, c in ipairs(s.cursors or {}) do\n    if c.id == f.id then\n      who = c\n    end\n  end\n  if not who then\n    return stop_following(s, \"they left\")\n  end\n  if not who.row or api.nvim_get_current_buf() ~= s.buf then\n    return\n  end\n  local win = api.nvim_get_current_win()\n  local row = math.min(who.row + 1, api.nvim_buf_line_count(s.buf))\n  pcall(api.nvim_win_set_cursor, win, { row, who.col or 0 })\n  api.nvim_win_call(win, function()\n    if row < vim.fn.line(\"w0\") or row > vim.fn.line(\"w$\") then\n      vim.cmd(\"normal! zz\")\n    end\n  end)\nend\n\n--- Follow someone's cursor: your view moves with it until you press a key.\n---@param buf? integer\n---@param name? string a name (or the start of one); nil: the only other person, else ask\nfunction M.follow(buf, name)\n  local s = M.session(buf)\n  if not s then\n    return notify(\"not a hedgesync buffer\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\n  end\n  name = vim.trim(name or \"\")\n  if s.follow and name == \"\" then\n    return stop_following(s, \"as asked\")\n  end\n  local candidates = vim.tbl_filter(function(c)\n    return name == \"\" or c.name:lower():find(name:lower(), 1, true) == 1\n  end, s.cursors or {})\n  local function start(c)\n    s.follow = { id = c.id, name = c.name }\n    -- While following, stay invisible: your cursor is theirs anyway.\n    send(s, { t = \"cursor\", row = vim.NIL })\n    vim.on_key(function(key)\n      if api.nvim_get_mode().mode:sub(1, 1) == \"c\" or key == \":\" then\n        return -- running a command (:Hedge users) keeps following\n      end\n      vim.schedule(function()\n        stop_following(s, \"you moved\")\n      end)\n    end, follow_ns)\n    notify((\"following %s; any key stops\"):format(c.name))\n    follow_update(s)\n  end\n  if #candidates == 0 then\n    notify(name == \"\" and \"nobody else is in this note\" or (\"nobody called \" .. name .. \" is here\"), vim.log.levels.WARN)\n  elseif #candidates == 1 then\n    start(candidates[1])\n  else\n    vim.ui.select(candidates, {\n      prompt = \"Follow\",\n      format_item = function(c)\n        return c.name .. (c.row and (\" (line \" .. (c.row + 1) .. \")\") or \"\")\n      end,\n    }, function(c)\n      if c then\n        start(c)\n      end\n    end)\n  end\nend\n\n--- Names of the others in the note, for completion.\nfunction M.names(buf)\n  local s = M.session(buf)\n  return vim.tbl_map(function(c)\n    return c.name\n  end, s and s.cursors or {})\nend\n\nlocal function on_reset(s, msg)\n  flush(s) -- dropped anyway (new epoch), but keeps the snapshot honest\n  local buf = s.buf\n  local first = not s.loaded\n  local view = vim.fn.bufwinid(buf) ~= -1 and vim.fn.winsaveview() or nil\n  local undolevels = vim.bo[buf].undolevels\n  if first then\n    vim.bo[buf].undolevels = -1 -- loading the note is not an undoable change\n  end\n  apply(s, function()\n    local text = vim.split(msg.text, \"\\n\", { plain = true })\n    if first then\n      -- Like reading a file: do not shift marks and quickfix entries that\n      -- already point into the note (`:cfirst`, `+42`) by the inserted lines.\n      vim.g._hedgesync_load = text\n      api.nvim_buf_call(buf, function()\n        vim.cmd(\"lockmarks call nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, v:false, g:_hedgesync_load)\")\n      end)\n      vim.g._hedgesync_load = nil\n    else\n      api.nvim_buf_set_lines(buf, 0, -1, false, text)\n    end\n  end)\n  if first then\n    vim.bo[buf].undolevels = undolevels\n  end\n  s.epoch, s.E, s.R, s.loaded = msg.epoch, 0, msg.seq, true\n  if view and not first and api.nvim_get_current_buf() == buf then\n    pcall(vim.fn.winrestview, view)\n  end\n  if first and s.goto_line then\n    for _, win in ipairs(vim.fn.win_findbuf(buf)) do\n      pcall(api.nvim_win_set_cursor, win, { math.min(s.goto_line, api.nvim_buf_line_count(buf)), 0 })\n    end\n    s.goto_line = nil\n  end\nend\n\nlocal function on_edit(s, msg)\n  flush(s) -- unreported local changes make this edit stale\n  if msg.base ~= s.E then\n    return -- typed something since; the bridge will resend this rebased\n  end\n  local ok, err = apply(s, function()\n    for _, e in ipairs(msg.edits) do\n      api.nvim_buf_set_text(s.buf, e.sr, e.sc, e.er, e.ec, vim.split(e.text, \"\\n\", { plain = true }))\n    end\n  end)\n  if not ok then\n    notify(\"could not apply a remote edit (\" .. tostring(err) .. \"); resyncing\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\n    send(s, { t = \"desync\" })\n    return\n  end\n  s.R = msg.seq\nend\n\n--- Why a bridge with protocol `theirs` cannot be used, and what to do.\nlocal function protocol_problem(theirs, version)\n  local fix = (theirs or 0) < M.protocol and \"update the hedgesync CLI\"\n    or \"run `hedgesync editor nvim install` to update this plugin\"\n  return (\"hedgesync %s speaks editor protocol %s, this plugin speaks %d: %s\"):format(\n    version or \"(unknown version)\",\n    tostring(theirs or \"none\"),\n    M.protocol,\n    fix\n  )\nend\nM._protocol_problem = protocol_problem\n\nlocal handlers = {\n  ready = function(s, msg)\n    if msg.protocol ~= M.protocol then\n      notify(protocol_problem(msg.protocol, msg.version), vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n      M.close(s.buf)\n      return\n    end\n    s.editable = msg.editable\n    s.title = msg.title\n    vim.b[s.buf].hedgesync_title = msg.title\n    set_modifiable(s)\n    update_status(s, \"connected\")\n    if not msg.editable then\n      notify(\"read-only, \" .. (msg.reason or \"you cannot edit this note\"), vim.log.levels.WARN)\n    end\n  end,\n  note = function(s, msg)\n    s.title = msg.title\n    vim.b[s.buf].hedgesync_title = msg.title\n    if msg.editable ~= s.editable then\n      s.editable = msg.editable\n      set_modifiable(s)\n      notify(\n        msg.editable and \"note is editable again\" or (\"now read-only, \" .. (msg.reason or \"you cannot edit this note\")),\n        vim.log.levels.WARN\n      )\n    end\n  end,\n  reset = on_reset,\n  edit = on_edit,\n  cursors = function(s, msg)\n    s.cursors = msg.cursors\n    draw_cursors(s, msg.cursors)\n    follow_update(s)\n  end,\n  status = function(s, msg)\n    if msg.state == \"desync\" then\n      notify(msg.message or \"buffer resynchronised\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\n    else\n      if msg.state == \"disconnected\" then\n        notify(\"offline; edits sync when reconnected\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\n      elseif msg.state == \"connected\" and s.state ~= \"connected\" then\n        notify(\"reconnected\")\n      end\n      update_status(s, msg.state)\n    end\n  end,\n  error = function(s, msg)\n    notify(msg.message, vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n  end,\n}\n\nlocal function dispatch(s, line)\n  local ok, msg = pcall(vim.json.decode, line, { luanil = { object = true, array = true } })\n  if not ok or type(msg) ~= \"table\" then\n    return\n  end\n  local handler = handlers[msg.t]\n  if handler and api.nvim_buf_is_valid(s.buf) then\n    handler(s, msg)\n  end\nend\n\n-- Buffer events ------------------------------------------------------------\n\nlocal function attach(s)\n  api.nvim_buf_attach(s.buf, false, {\n    on_bytes = function()\n      if s.closed then\n        return true -- detach\n      end\n      if s.applying or not s.loaded then\n        return\n      end\n      if not s.dirty then\n        s.dirty = true\n        vim.schedule(function()\n          flush(s)\n        end)\n      end\n    end,\n    on_detach = function()\n      s.closed = true\n    end,\n  })\n\n  local group = api.nvim_create_augroup(\"hedgesync_buf_\" .. s.buf, { clear = true })\n  local timer = vim.uv.new_timer()\n  s.cursor_timer = timer\n  local function send_cursor()\n    if not s.loaded or api.nvim_get_current_buf() ~= s.buf or s.follow then\n      return\n    end\n    flush(s)\n    local pos = api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\n    send(s, { t = \"cursor\", epoch = s.epoch, seen = s.R, row = pos[1] - 1, col = pos[2] })\n  end\n  api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"CursorMoved\", \"CursorMovedI\" }, {\n    group = group,\n    buffer = s.buf,\n    callback = function()\n      timer:stop()\n      timer:start(M.config.cursor_debounce, 0, vim.schedule_wrap(send_cursor))\n    end,\n  })\n  s.send_cursor = send_cursor\n  api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufEnter\", { group = group, buffer = s.buf, callback = send_cursor })\n  api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufLeave\", {\n    group = group,\n    buffer = s.buf,\n    callback = function()\n      stop_following(s, \"you left the buffer\")\n      send(s, { t = \"cursor\", row = vim.NIL })\n    end,\n  })\n  api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufWriteCmd\", {\n    group = group,\n    buffer = s.buf,\n    callback = function()\n      vim.bo[s.buf].modified = false\n      notify(s.state == \"connected\" and \"changes are synced live\" or (\"not connected (\" .. tostring(s.state) .. \")\"))\n    end,\n  })\n  api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"BufWipeout\", \"BufDelete\" }, {\n    group = group,\n    buffer = s.buf,\n    callback = function()\n      M.close(s.buf)\n    end,\n  })\nend\n\n-- Public API ---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n--- hedgedoc://host/id -> https://host/id (http for localhost)\nfunction M.http_url(url)\n  url = vim.trim(url or \"\")\n  if url:match(\"^hedgedoc://\") then\n    local rest = url:gsub(\"^hedgedoc://\", \"\")\n    local scheme = (rest:match(\"^localhost\") or rest:match(\"^127%.\")) and \"http://\" or \"https://\"\n    return scheme .. rest\n  end\n  return url\nend\n\n--- The buffer name for a note: https://host/id -> hedgedoc://host/id\nlocal function buf_name(url)\n  return \"hedgedoc://\" .. url:gsub(\"^https?://\", \"\")\nend\nM.buf_name = buf_name\n\n--- Open a note for live editing in the current window. Returns the buffer.\n--- Open a note for live editing in a buffer.\n---@param url string note URL (https://... or hedgedoc://...)\n---@param opts? { line?: integer, buf?: integer, wait?: integer }\n---  line: put the cursor there once the note is loaded\n---  buf: load into this buffer in place (BufReadCmd); no window changes\n---  wait: block up to this many ms until the note is loaded, like reading a file\nfunction M.open(url, opts)\n  opts = opts or {}\n  url = M.http_url(url)\n  if url == \"\" then\n    notify(\"usage: :Hedge open <note url>\", vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n    return\n  end\n  for buf, s in pairs(sessions) do\n    if s.url == url and api.nvim_buf_is_valid(buf) then\n      api.nvim_set_current_buf(buf)\n      if opts.line then\n        pcall(api.nvim_win_set_cursor, 0, { opts.line, 0 })\n      end\n      return buf\n    end\n  end\n\n  local prev = api.nvim_get_current_buf()\n  local name = buf_name(url)\n  local buf = opts.buf\n  if not buf then\n    for _, b in ipairs(api.nvim_list_bufs()) do\n      if api.nvim_buf_get_name(b) == name then\n        buf = b\n      end\n    end\n  end\n  if not buf or not api.nvim_buf_is_valid(buf) then\n    buf = api.nvim_create_buf(true, false)\n    api.nvim_buf_set_name(buf, name)\n  end\n  vim.bo[buf].buftype = \"acwrite\"\n  vim.bo[buf].swapfile = false\n  vim.bo[buf].modifiable = false\n  vim.bo[buf].filetype = \"markdown\"\n  if not opts.buf then\n    api.nvim_set_current_buf(buf)\n  end\n  -- Replace the empty buffer Neovim starts with (`hedgesync edit`, a fresh :Hedge open).\n  if\n    not opts.buf\n    and prev ~= buf\n    and api.nvim_buf_get_name(prev) == \"\"\n    and vim.bo[prev].buftype == \"\"\n    and not vim.bo[prev].modified\n    and api.nvim_buf_line_count(prev) == 1\n    and api.nvim_buf_get_lines(prev, 0, 1, false)[1] == \"\"\n  then\n    pcall(api.nvim_buf_delete, prev, {})\n  end\n\n  local s = {\n    buf = buf,\n    url = url,\n    E = 0,\n    R = 0,\n    epoch = 0,\n    loaded = false,\n    editable = false,\n    state = \"connecting\",\n    lines = {},\n    goto_line = opts.line,\n  }\n  sessions[buf] = s\n  update_status(s, \"connecting\")\n  attach(s)\n\n  local cmd = vim.list_extend(vim.list_extend(vim.deepcopy(M.config.cmd), { \"bridge\", url }), M.config.args)\n  local pending = \"\"\n  local stderr = {}\n  local ok, proc = pcall(vim.system, cmd, {\n    stdin = true,\n    stdout = function(_, data)\n      if not data then\n        return\n      end\n      pending = pending .. data\n      local lines = vim.split(pending, \"\\n\", { plain = true })\n      pending = table.remove(lines)\n      for _, line in ipairs(lines) do\n        if line ~= \"\" then\n          vim.schedule(function()\n            dispatch(s, line)\n          end)\n        end\n      end\n    end,\n    stderr = function(_, data)\n      if data then\n        table.insert(stderr, data)\n      end\n    end,\n  }, function(result)\n    vim.schedule(function()\n      local was_closed = s.closed\n      s.closed = true\n      s.proc = nil\n      if api.nvim_buf_is_valid(buf) then\n        set_modifiable(s)\n        update_status(s, \"closed\")\n        api.nvim_buf_clear_namespace(buf, ns, 0, -1)\n      end\n      if not was_closed and result.code ~= 0 then\n        local err = vim.trim(table.concat(stderr))\n        if err:find(\"Unknown command: bridge\", 1, true) then\n          notify(\"your hedgesync CLI is too old for this plugin (no `bridge` command); update it\", vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n          return\n        end\n        notify(\"bridge exited (\" .. result.code .. \")\" .. (err ~= \"\" and (\":\\n\" .. err) or \"\"), vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n      end\n    end)\n  end)\n  if not ok then\n    sessions[buf] = nil\n    notify(\"could not start \" .. table.concat(cmd, \" \") .. \": \" .. tostring(proc), vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n    return\n  end\n  s.proc = proc\n  if opts.wait then\n    vim.wait(opts.wait, function()\n      return s.loaded or s.closed\n    end, 10)\n  end\n  return buf\nend\n\n--- Stop syncing a buffer (edits made so far are flushed by the bridge).\nfunction M.close(buf)\n  buf = (buf == nil or buf == 0) and api.nvim_get_current_buf() or buf\n  local s = sessions[buf]\n  if not s then\n    return\n  end\n  stop_following(s)\n  sessions[buf] = nil\n  if s.cursor_timer then\n    s.cursor_timer:stop()\n    s.cursor_timer:close()\n  end\n  if s.proc and not s.closed then\n    flush(s)\n    send(s, { t = \"close\" })\n    pcall(function()\n      s.proc:write(nil)\n    end)\n  end\n  s.closed = true\n  if api.nvim_buf_is_valid(buf) then\n    pcall(api.nvim_buf_clear_namespace, buf, ns, 0, -1)\n    pcall(api.nvim_del_augroup_by_name, \"hedgesync_buf_\" .. buf)\n    vim.bo[buf].modifiable = false\n  end\nend\n\n--- Close all sessions and wait (briefly) for the bridges to flush.\nfunction M.close_all(timeout)\n  local procs = {}\n  for buf, s in pairs(sessions) do\n    if s.proc then\n      table.insert(procs, s.proc)\n    end\n    M.close(buf)\n  end\n  for _, proc in ipairs(procs) do\n    pcall(function()\n      proc:wait(timeout or 3000)\n    end)\n  end\nend\n\n--- Session for a buffer (for statuslines and tests).\n--- Every open note session, by buffer.\nfunction M.sessions()\n  return sessions\nend\n\nfunction M.session(buf)\n  return sessions[(buf == nil or buf == 0) and api.nvim_get_current_buf() or buf]\nend\n\n--- Short status for statuslines, e.g. \"● connected\".\nfunction M.status(buf)\n  local s = M.session(buf)\n  if not s then\n    return \"\"\n  end\n  local icon = ({ connected = \"●\", connecting = \"◌\", reconnecting = \"◌\", disconnected = \"○\", closed = \"×\" })[s.state]\n    or \"?\"\n  return icon .. \" \" .. tostring(s.state) .. (s.follow and (\" · following \" .. s.follow.name) or \"\")\nend\n\nfunction M.users(buf)\n  local s = M.session(buf)\n  if not s then\n    notify(\"not a hedgesync buffer\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\n    return\n  end\n  local names = {}\n  for _, c in ipairs(s.cursors or {}) do\n    table.insert(names, c.row and (\"%s (line %d)\"):format(c.name, c.row + 1) or c.name)\n  end\n  notify(#names > 0 and (\"also here: \" .. table.concat(names, \", \")) or \"nobody else is in this note\")\nend\n\nfunction M.setup(opts)\n  M.config = vim.tbl_deep_extend(\"force\", M.config, opts or {})\nend\n\nreturn M\n",
  "lua/hedgesync/ui.lua": "-- hedgesync.nvim: browsing notes, creating them, search and revisions.\n--\n-- Everything here goes through the CLI's --json output (`hedgesync list`,\n-- `create`, `search`, `revisions`, ...), so it uses the same saved logins and\n-- needs no HTTP code of its own. Live editing stays in init.lua.\n\nlocal M = {}\nlocal api = vim.api\nlocal function hs()\n  return require(\"hedgesync\")\nend\n\nlocal function notify(msg, level)\n  vim.notify(\"hedgesync: \" .. msg, level or vim.log.levels.INFO)\nend\n\n---@type table<integer, table> state of browse/revisions buffers, by buffer\nlocal views = {}\nlocal ns = api.nvim_create_namespace(\"hedgesync_ui\")\n\nfor name, link in pairs({\n  HedgeSyncHeader = \"Title\",\n  HedgeSyncPinned = \"DiagnosticWarn\",\n  HedgeSyncTag = \"Label\",\n  HedgeSyncTime = \"Comment\",\n  HedgeSyncHint = \"Comment\",\n  HedgeSyncAdded = \"Added\",\n  HedgeSyncRemoved = \"Removed\",\n}) do\n  api.nvim_set_hl(0, name, { link = link, default = true })\nend\n\n--- Run `hedgesync <args> --json` and call on_ok(data) on the main loop.\n--- Failures are reported (with the CLI's hint) and call opts.on_error.\n---@param args string[]\n---@param on_ok fun(data: table)\n---@param opts? { stdin?: string, on_error?: fun() }\nfunction M.cli(args, on_ok, opts)\n  opts = opts or {}\n  local cmd = vim.list_extend(vim.deepcopy(hs().config.cmd), args)\n  table.insert(cmd, \"--json\")\n  local ok, err = pcall(vim.system, cmd, { text = true, stdin = opts.stdin or false }, function(r)\n    vim.schedule(function()\n      local decoded, data = pcall(vim.json.decode, r.stdout or \"\")\n      if decoded and type(data) == \"table\" and data.success ~= false then\n        return on_ok(data)\n      end\n      local msg = decoded and type(data) == \"table\" and data.error or vim.trim(r.stderr or \"\")\n      if msg == \"\" then\n        msg = (\"`hedgesync %s` failed (exit %d)\"):format(args[1], r.code)\n      end\n      local hint = decoded and type(data) == \"table\" and data.hint\n      notify(msg .. (hint and (\"\\n\" .. hint) or \"\"), vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n      if opts.on_error then\n        opts.on_error()\n      end\n    end)\n  end)\n  if not ok then\n    notify(\"could not run \" .. cmd[1] .. \": \" .. tostring(err), vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n  end\nend\n\n--- https://host[/sub]/id -> https://host[/sub]\nfunction M.server_of(url)\n  return (url:gsub(\"[?#].*$\", \"\"):gsub(\"/+$\", \"\"):match(\"^(.-)/[^/]+$\"))\nend\n\nlocal function normalize_server(s)\n  s = hs().http_url(s)\n  if not s:match(\"^https?://\") then\n    s = \"https://\" .. s\n  end\n  return (s:gsub(\"/+$\", \"\"))\nend\n\n--- The server to work with: the argument, the note or view in the current\n--- buffer, the last one used, the only saved login, else ask.\n---@param arg string|nil\n---@param cb fun(server: string)\nfunction M.pick_server(arg, cb)\n  arg = vim.trim(arg or \"\")\n  if arg ~= \"\" then\n    M.last_server = normalize_server(arg)\n    return cb(M.last_server)\n  end\n  local s = hs().session(0)\n  local view = views[api.nvim_get_current_buf()]\n  local here = s and M.server_of(s.url) or view and view.server\n  if here then\n    M.last_server = here\n    return cb(here)\n  end\n  if M.last_server then\n    return cb(M.last_server)\n  end\n  -- The server of the notes open right now, if they share one.\n  local open = {}\n  for _, other in pairs(hs().sessions()) do\n    open[M.server_of(other.url)] = true\n  end\n  if vim.tbl_count(open) == 1 then\n    M.last_server = next(open)\n    return cb(M.last_server)\n  end\n  M.cli({ \"sessions\" }, function(data)\n    local list = data.sessions or {}\n    if #list == 0 then\n      notify(\"no saved login; run: hedgesync login <server> --save (or pass a server)\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\n    elseif #list == 1 then\n      M.last_server = list[1].server\n      cb(list[1].server)\n    else\n      vim.ui.select(list, {\n        prompt = \"HedgeDoc server\",\n        format_item = function(x)\n          return x.server .. (x.user and x.user.name and (\"  (\" .. x.user.name .. \")\") or \"\")\n        end,\n      }, function(choice)\n        if choice then\n          M.last_server = choice.server\n          cb(choice.server)\n        end\n      end)\n    end\n  end)\nend\n\nlocal function relative(ms)\n  local d = os.time() - math.floor((ms or 0) / 1000)\n  if d < 60 then\n    return \"just now\"\n  elseif d < 3600 then\n    return (\"%d min ago\"):format(d / 60)\n  elseif d < 86400 then\n    return (\"%d h ago\"):format(d / 3600)\n  elseif d < 86400 * 30 then\n    local days = math.floor(d / 86400)\n    return days == 1 and \"yesterday\" or (\"%d days ago\"):format(days)\n  end\n  return os.date(\"%Y-%m-%d\", math.floor(ms / 1000))\nend\n\nlocal function pad(text, width)\n  local w = vim.fn.strdisplaywidth(text)\n  if w > width then\n    text = vim.fn.strcharpart(text, 0, width - 1) .. \"…\"\n    w = vim.fn.strdisplaywidth(text)\n  end\n  return text .. string.rep(\" \", width - w)\nend\n\nlocal function find_buf(name)\n  for _, b in ipairs(api.nvim_list_bufs()) do\n    if api.nvim_buf_get_name(b) == name then\n      return b\n    end\n  end\nend\n\n--- A scratch buffer for a view, reused by name, shown in the current window.\nlocal function view_buf(name, filetype)\n  local buf = find_buf(name)\n  if not buf then\n    buf = api.nvim_create_buf(true, true)\n    api.nvim_buf_set_name(buf, name)\n    vim.bo[buf].buftype = \"nofile\"\n    vim.bo[buf].bufhidden = \"hide\"\n    vim.bo[buf].swapfile = false\n    vim.bo[buf].filetype = filetype\n  end\n  api.nvim_set_current_buf(buf)\n  vim.wo.wrap = false\n  vim.wo.cursorline = true\n  return buf\nend\n\n--- Replace a view's lines; marks are {row, col_start, col_end, hl_group} (0-based bytes).\nlocal function render(buf, lines, marks)\n  vim.bo[buf].modifiable = true\n  api.nvim_buf_set_lines(buf, 0, -1, false, lines)\n  vim.bo[buf].modifiable = false\n  vim.bo[buf].modified = false\n  api.nvim_buf_clear_namespace(buf, ns, 0, -1)\n  for _, m in ipairs(marks or {}) do\n    pcall(api.nvim_buf_set_extmark, buf, ns, m[1], m[2], { end_col = m[3], hl_group = m[4] })\n  end\nend\n\nlocal function map(buf, lhs, fn, desc)\n  vim.keymap.set(\"n\", lhs, fn, { buffer = buf, nowait = true, silent = true, desc = \"hedgesync: \" .. desc })\nend\n\n--- Put text in the clipboard (if Neovim has one) and the unnamed register.\nlocal function set_clipboard(text)\n  -- Without a provider, setting \"+ prints an error that, stacked with our\n  -- message, raises a hit-enter prompt, which holds up remote edits.\n  if vim.fn.has(\"clipboard\") == 1 then\n    pcall(vim.fn.setreg, \"+\", text)\n  end\n  vim.fn.setreg('\"', text)\nend\n\nlocal function copy(text)\n  set_clipboard(text)\n  notify(\"copied \" .. text)\nend\n\nlocal function item_under_cursor(buf)\n  local view = views[buf]\n  if not view or not view.items then\n    return\n  end\n  return view.items[api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)[1] - view.first + 1]\nend\n\n--- The note a command is about: the live note in this buffer, or the note\n--- under the cursor in a browse view.\nlocal function current_note()\n  local s = hs().session(0)\n  if s then\n    return { url = s.url, title = s.title }\n  end\n  local view = views[api.nvim_get_current_buf()]\n  if view and view.kind == \"browse\" then\n    local item = item_under_cursor(api.nvim_get_current_buf())\n    return item and { url = item.url, title = item.text }\n  elseif view and view.kind == \"revisions\" then\n    return { url = view.url, title = view.title }\n  end\nend\n\nlocal function help(lines)\n  notify(\"keys\\n\" .. table.concat(lines, \"\\n\"))\nend\n\n-- :Hedge browse ---------------------------------------------------------\n\nlocal browse_help = {\n  \"<CR> open        <C-v> open in vsplit   <C-x> open in split\",\n  \"n    new note    p     pin / unpin      r     revisions\",\n  \"y    copy URL    D     remove from history\",\n  \"s    search text (quickfix)             R     reload      q close\",\n}\n\nlocal function draw_browse(buf)\n  local view = views[buf]\n  local lines = { \"\", \"\" }\n  local marks = {}\n  local count = view.items and #view.items or 0\n  lines[1] = view.items and (\"%s · %d note%s · ? for keys\"):format(view.server, count, count == 1 and \"\" or \"s\")\n    or (view.server .. \" · loading…\")\n  marks[1] = { 0, 0, #view.server, \"HedgeSyncHeader\" }\n  if view.items and count == 0 then\n    table.insert(lines, \"  (your history is empty: notes appear here once you have opened them while signed in)\")\n  end\n  local width = 20\n  for _, item in ipairs(view.items or {}) do\n    width = math.max(width, math.min(50, vim.fn.strdisplaywidth(item.text or \"\")))\n  end\n  for _, item in ipairs(view.items or {}) do\n    local pin = item.pinned and \"★ \" or \"  \"\n    local title = pad(item.text ~= \"\" and item.text or \"(untitled)\", width)\n    local time = pad(relative(item.time), 12)\n    local tags = {}\n    for _, t in ipairs(item.tags or {}) do\n      table.insert(tags, \"#\" .. t)\n    end\n    local line = pin .. title .. \"  \" .. time .. \"  \" .. table.concat(tags, \" \")\n    local row = #lines\n    table.insert(lines, line)\n    if item.pinned then\n      table.insert(marks, { row, 0, #pin, \"HedgeSyncPinned\" })\n    end\n    local t0 = #pin + #title + 2\n    table.insert(marks, { row, t0, t0 + #time, \"HedgeSyncTime\" })\n    table.insert(marks, { row, t0 + #time + 2, #line, \"HedgeSyncTag\" })\n  end\n  render(buf, lines, marks)\nend\n\nlocal function load_browse(buf, keep_cursor)\n  local view = views[buf]\n  local cursor = keep_cursor and api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\n  M.cli({ \"list\", view.server }, function(data)\n    if not api.nvim_buf_is_valid(buf) then\n      return\n    end\n    view.items = data.notes or {}\n    draw_browse(buf)\n    for _, win in ipairs(vim.fn.win_findbuf(buf)) do\n      local row = cursor and cursor[1] or view.first\n      pcall(api.nvim_win_set_cursor, win, { math.min(row, api.nvim_buf_line_count(buf)), 0 })\n    end\n  end)\nend\n\n--- List the notes in your history on a server; open, pin, create, search.\nfunction M.browse(server)\n  M.pick_server(server, function(srv)\n    local buf = view_buf(\"hedgesync://browse/\" .. srv:gsub(\"^https?://\", \"\"), \"hedgesync_browse\")\n    local fresh = not views[buf]\n    views[buf] = views[buf] or { kind = \"browse\", server = srv, first = 3 }\n    if fresh then\n      draw_browse(buf)\n      local function open_with(cmd)\n        return function()\n          local item = item_under_cursor(buf)\n          if item then\n            if cmd then\n              vim.cmd(cmd)\n            end\n            hs().open(item.url)\n          end\n        end\n      end\n      map(buf, \"<CR>\", open_with(nil), \"open note\")\n      map(buf, \"<C-v>\", open_with(\"vsplit\"), \"open note in a vertical split\")\n      map(buf, \"<C-x>\", open_with(\"split\"), \"open note in a split\")\n      map(buf, \"n\", function()\n        M.new({ server = srv })\n      end, \"new note\")\n      map(buf, \"p\", function()\n        local item = item_under_cursor(buf)\n        if item then\n          M.cli({ item.pinned and \"unpin\" or \"pin\", item.url }, function()\n            load_browse(buf, true)\n          end)\n        end\n      end, \"pin or unpin\")\n      map(buf, \"r\", function()\n        local item = item_under_cursor(buf)\n        if item then\n          M.revisions(item.url, item.text)\n        end\n      end, \"revisions\")\n      map(buf, \"y\", function()\n        local item = item_under_cursor(buf)\n        if item then\n          copy(item.url)\n        end\n      end, \"copy URL\")\n      map(buf, \"D\", function()\n        local item = item_under_cursor(buf)\n        if item and vim.fn.confirm((\"Remove “%s” from your history? (The note itself stays.)\"):format(item.text), \"&Remove\\n&Cancel\", 2) == 1 then\n          M.cli({ \"history-delete\", item.url }, function()\n            load_browse(buf, true)\n          end)\n        end\n      end, \"remove from history\")\n      map(buf, \"s\", function()\n        vim.ui.input({ prompt = \"Search your notes for: \" }, function(text)\n          if text and vim.trim(text) ~= \"\" then\n            M.search(text, srv)\n          end\n        end)\n      end, \"search note text\")\n      map(buf, \"R\", function()\n        load_browse(buf, true)\n      end, \"reload\")\n      map(buf, \"q\", function()\n        vim.cmd(\"bdelete\")\n      end, \"close\")\n      map(buf, \"?\", function()\n        help(browse_help)\n      end, \"help\")\n    end\n    load_browse(buf, not fresh)\n  end)\nend\n\n-- :Hedge find -----------------------------------------------------------\n\n--- Pick a note from your history with vim.ui.select (your fuzzy finder, if it replaces it).\nfunction M.find(server)\n  M.pick_server(server, function(srv)\n    M.cli({ \"list\", srv }, function(data)\n      local notes = data.notes or {}\n      if #notes == 0 then\n        return notify(\"no notes in your history on \" .. srv)\n      end\n      vim.ui.select(notes, {\n        prompt = \"Open note\",\n        format_item = function(n)\n          local tags = {}\n          for _, t in ipairs(n.tags or {}) do\n            table.insert(tags, \"#\" .. t)\n          end\n          return (n.pinned and \"★ \" or \"\") .. (n.text ~= \"\" and n.text or n.id) .. \"  \" .. table.concat(tags, \" \")\n        end,\n      }, function(choice)\n        if choice then\n          hs().open(choice.url)\n        end\n      end)\n    end)\n  end)\nend\n\n-- :Hedge new ------------------------------------------------------------\n\n--- Create a note and open it. With lines, they become its content; with a\n--- title, it starts with \"# title\".\n---@param opts { server?: string, title?: string, lines?: string[] }\nfunction M.new(opts)\n  opts = opts or {}\n  M.pick_server(opts.server, function(srv)\n    local function create(title)\n      local content, line = \"\", nil\n      if opts.lines then\n        content = table.concat(opts.lines, \"\\n\") .. \"\\n\"\n      elseif title ~= \"\" then\n        content, line = \"# \" .. title .. \"\\n\\n\", 3\n      end\n      M.cli({ \"create\", srv }, function(data)\n        notify(\"created \" .. data.url)\n        hs().open(data.url, { line = line })\n      end, { stdin = content })\n    end\n    if opts.title or opts.lines then\n      create(opts.title or \"\")\n    else\n      vim.ui.input({ prompt = \"Title of the new note (empty for none): \" }, function(title)\n        if title then\n          create(vim.trim(title))\n        end\n      end)\n    end\n  end)\nend\n\n-- :Hedge search ---------------------------------------------------------\n\n--- Search the text of your notes; matches go to the quickfix list, whose\n--- entries open the notes live at the matching line.\nfunction M.search(pattern, server)\n  pattern = vim.trim(pattern or \"\")\n  if pattern == \"\" then\n    return notify(\"usage: :Hedge search <text>\", vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n  end\n  M.pick_server(server, function(srv)\n    notify(\"searching your notes on \" .. srv .. \"…\")\n    local args = { \"search\", srv, pattern }\n    if pattern:lower() == pattern then\n      table.insert(args, \"--ignore-case\") -- smartcase\n    end\n    M.cli(args, function(data)\n      local items = {}\n      for _, n in ipairs(data.notes or {}) do\n        for _, l in ipairs(n.lines or {}) do\n          table.insert(items, { filename = hs().buf_name(n.url), lnum = l.line, text = n.title .. \" │ \" .. l.text })\n        end\n      end\n      vim.fn.setqflist({}, \" \", { title = \"hedgesync search: \" .. pattern, items = items })\n      if #items == 0 then\n        notify((\"no matches in %d notes\"):format(data.searched or 0))\n      else\n        vim.cmd(\"botright copen\")\n      end\n    end)\n  end)\nend\n\n-- :Hedge revisions --------------------------------------------------------\n\nlocal revisions_help = {\n  \"<CR> view revision    d diff with the note    R restore into the note\",\n  \"y    copy timestamp   r reload                 q close\",\n}\n\n--- A read-only buffer with one revision's content.\nlocal function show_revision(view, rev, cb)\n  local name = (\"hedgesync://revision/%s@%d\"):format(view.url:gsub(\"^https?://\", \"\"), rev.time)\n  local function done(buf)\n    if cb then\n      cb(buf)\n    end\n  end\n  local existing = find_buf(name)\n  if existing then\n    return done(existing)\n  end\n  M.cli({ \"revisions\", view.url, tostring(rev.time) }, function(data)\n    local buf = find_buf(name) or api.nvim_create_buf(true, true)\n    api.nvim_buf_set_name(buf, name)\n    vim.bo[buf].buftype = \"nofile\"\n    vim.bo[buf].bufhidden = \"wipe\"\n    vim.bo[buf].swapfile = false\n    api.nvim_buf_set_lines(buf, 0, -1, false, vim.split(data.content or \"\", \"\\n\", { plain = true }))\n    vim.bo[buf].modifiable = false\n    vim.bo[buf].filetype = \"markdown\"\n    map(buf, \"q\", function()\n      local diffing = vim.wo.diff\n      vim.cmd(\"close\")\n      if diffing then\n        vim.cmd(\"diffoff!\")\n      end\n    end, \"close revision\")\n    done(buf)\n  end)\nend\n\nlocal function revision_under_cursor(buf)\n  local view = views[buf]\n  local i = api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)[1] - view.first + 1\n  return view.items and view.items[i], i - 1\nend\n\n--- The window showing the live note, opening it in another window if needed.\nlocal function note_window(url, list_win)\n  local name = hs().buf_name(url)\n  local buf = find_buf(name)\n  if buf then\n    local wins = vim.fn.win_findbuf(buf)\n    if #wins > 0 then\n      return wins[1]\n    end\n  end\n  api.nvim_set_current_win(list_win)\n  vim.cmd(\"aboveleft split\")\n  hs().open(url)\n  return api.nvim_get_current_win()\nend\n\nlocal function draw_revisions(buf)\n  local view = views[buf]\n  local header = (\"Revisions of %s\"):format(view.title ~= nil and view.title ~= \"\" and view.title or view.url)\n  local lines = { header .. \" · ? for keys\", \"\" }\n  local marks = { { 0, 0, #header, \"HedgeSyncHeader\" } }\n  if view.items and #view.items == 0 then\n    table.insert(lines, \"  (no revisions yet; HedgeDoc saves them periodically while a note is edited)\")\n  elseif not view.items then\n    table.insert(lines, \"  loading…\")\n  end\n  for i, rev in ipairs(view.items or {}) do\n    local older = view.items[i + 1]\n    local delta = older and (rev.length - older.length) or nil\n    local head = (\"~%-3d %s  %s %7d chars\"):format(\n      i - 1,\n      os.date(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\", math.floor(rev.time / 1000)),\n      pad(relative(rev.time), 12),\n      rev.length\n    )\n    local tail = delta == nil and \"\" or delta == 0 and \"  ±0\" or (\"  %+d\"):format(delta)\n    local row = #lines\n    table.insert(lines, head .. tail)\n    table.insert(marks, { row, 23, 23 + 12, \"HedgeSyncTime\" })\n    if delta and delta ~= 0 then\n      table.insert(marks, { row, #head, #head + #tail, delta > 0 and \"HedgeSyncAdded\" or \"HedgeSyncRemoved\" })\n    end\n  end\n  render(buf, lines, marks)\nend\n\nlocal function load_revisions(buf)\n  local view = views[buf]\n  M.cli({ \"revisions\", view.url }, function(data)\n    if api.nvim_buf_is_valid(buf) then\n      view.items = data.revisions or {}\n      draw_revisions(buf)\n      for _, win in ipairs(vim.fn.win_findbuf(buf)) do\n        if api.nvim_win_get_cursor(win)[1] < view.first then\n          pcall(api.nvim_win_set_cursor, win, { math.min(view.first, api.nvim_buf_line_count(buf)), 0 })\n        end\n      end\n    end\n  end)\nend\n\nlocal function restore(view, rev, index)\n  local label = (\"~%d (%s)\"):format(index, os.date(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\", math.floor(rev.time / 1000)))\n  if vim.fn.confirm(\"Make the note's content revision \" .. label .. \" again?\", \"&Restore\\n&Cancel\", 2) ~= 1 then\n    return\n  end\n  local name = hs().buf_name(view.url)\n  local live = find_buf(name)\n  local s = live and hs().session(live)\n  if s and s.loaded and s.editable then\n    -- As an edit in the live buffer: synced like typing, and `u` undoes it.\n    M.cli({ \"revisions\", view.url, tostring(rev.time) }, function(data)\n      api.nvim_buf_set_lines(s.buf, 0, -1, false, vim.split(data.content or \"\", \"\\n\", { plain = true }))\n      notify(\"restored \" .. label .. \"; u in the note undoes it\")\n    end)\n  else\n    M.cli({ \"revisions\", view.url, tostring(rev.time), \"--restore\" }, function()\n      notify(\"restored \" .. label)\n    end)\n  end\nend\n\n--- List a note's revisions; view, diff against the note, or restore one.\n---@param url? string the note (default: the current one)\n---@param title? string\nfunction M.revisions(url, title)\n  if not url then\n    local note = current_note()\n    if not note then\n      return notify(\"not on a note: open one, or use this from :Hedge browse\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\n    end\n    url, title = note.url, note.title\n  end\n  if hs().session(0) then\n    vim.cmd(\"botright 12split\")\n  end\n  local list_win = api.nvim_get_current_win()\n  local buf = view_buf(\"hedgesync://revisions/\" .. url:gsub(\"^https?://\", \"\"), \"hedgesync_revisions\")\n  local fresh = not views[buf]\n  views[buf] = views[buf] or { kind = \"revisions\", url = url, server = M.server_of(url), first = 3 }\n  local view = views[buf]\n  view.title = title or view.title\n  if fresh then\n    draw_revisions(buf)\n    map(buf, \"<CR>\", function()\n      local rev = revision_under_cursor(buf)\n      if rev then\n        show_revision(view, rev, function(rbuf)\n          vim.cmd(\"aboveleft split\")\n          api.nvim_set_current_buf(rbuf)\n        end)\n      end\n    end, \"view revision\")\n    map(buf, \"d\", function()\n      local rev = revision_under_cursor(buf)\n      if not rev then\n        return\n      end\n      show_revision(view, rev, function(rbuf)\n        local win = note_window(view.url, list_win)\n        api.nvim_set_current_win(win)\n        vim.cmd(\"diffthis\")\n        vim.cmd(\"leftabove vsplit\")\n        api.nvim_set_current_buf(rbuf)\n        vim.cmd(\"diffthis\")\n      end)\n    end, \"diff with the note\")\n    map(buf, \"R\", function()\n      local rev, index = revision_under_cursor(buf)\n      if rev then\n        restore(view, rev, index)\n      end\n    end, \"restore revision\")\n    map(buf, \"y\", function()\n      local rev = revision_under_cursor(buf)\n      if rev then\n        copy(tostring(rev.time))\n      end\n    end, \"copy timestamp\")\n    map(buf, \"r\", function()\n      load_revisions(buf)\n    end, \"reload\")\n    map(buf, \"q\", function()\n      if #api.nvim_list_wins() > 1 then\n        vim.cmd(\"close\")\n      else\n        vim.cmd(\"bdelete\")\n      end\n    end, \"close\")\n    map(buf, \"?\", function()\n      help(revisions_help)\n    end, \"help\")\n  end\n  load_revisions(buf)\nend\n\n-- :Hedge url --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n--- Copy the note's URL: the editor (default), its published page or slides.\n---@param kind? \"edit\"|\"publish\"|\"slide\"\nfunction M.url(kind)\n  local note = current_note()\n  if not note then\n    return notify(\"not on a note\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\n  end\n  kind = vim.trim(kind or \"\")\n  if kind == \"\" or kind == \"edit\" then\n    return copy(note.url)\n  end\n  if kind ~= \"publish\" and kind ~= \"slide\" then\n    return notify(\"usage: :Hedge url [edit|publish|slide]\", vim.log.levels.ERROR)\n  end\n  M.cli({ \"publish\", note.url }, function(data)\n    copy(data[kind])\n  end)\nend\n\nM._views = views\nreturn M\n",
  "plugin/hedgesync.lua": "if vim.g.loaded_hedgesync then\n  return\nend\nvim.g.loaded_hedgesync = true\n\nlocal function ui()\n  return require(\"hedgesync.ui\")\nend\n\nlocal subcommands = {\n  open = function(args)\n    require(\"hedgesync\").open(args)\n  end,\n  browse = function(args)\n    ui().browse(args)\n  end,\n  find = function(args)\n    ui().find(args)\n  end,\n  new = function(args, opts)\n    local lines\n    if opts.range > 0 then\n      lines = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, opts.line1 - 1, opts.line2, false)\n    end\n    ui().new({ title = args ~= \"\" and args or nil, lines = lines })\n  end,\n  search = function(args)\n    ui().search(args)\n  end,\n  revisions = function()\n    ui().revisions()\n  end,\n  url = function(args)\n    ui().url(args)\n  end,\n  close = function()\n    require(\"hedgesync\").close(0)\n  end,\n  follow = function(args)\n    require(\"hedgesync\").follow(0, args)\n  end,\n  users = function()\n    require(\"hedgesync\").users(0)\n  end,\n  status = function()\n    vim.notify(require(\"hedgesync\").status(0))\n  end,\n}\n\nlocal usage = table.concat({\n  \"usage: :Hedge <command>\",\n  \"  open <url>        edit a note live (or :e hedgedoc://host/id)\",\n  \"  browse [server]   your notes: open, pin, create, revisions\",\n  \"  find [server]     pick a note with vim.ui.select\",\n  \"  new [title]       create a note and open it (with a range: from those lines)\",\n  \"  search <text>     search your notes' text into the quickfix list\",\n  \"  revisions         this note's revisions: view, diff, restore\",\n  \"  url [publish|slide]  copy this note's URL\",\n  \"  follow [name]     your view follows their cursor (any key stops; again to stop)\",\n  \"  users | status | close\",\n}, \"\\n\")\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_user_command(\"Hedge\", function(opts)\n  local sub, rest = opts.args:match(\"^(%S+)%s*(.*)$\")\n  local fn = subcommands[sub or \"\"]\n  if not fn then\n    vim.notify(usage, sub and vim.log.levels.ERROR or vim.log.levels.INFO)\n    return\n  end\n  fn(rest, opts)\nend, {\n  nargs = \"*\",\n  range = true,\n  complete = function(arglead, line)\n    if line:match(\"^%S+%s+%S*$\") then\n      local names = vim.tbl_keys(subcommands)\n      table.sort(names)\n      return vim.tbl_filter(function(name)\n        return name:find(arglead, 1, true) == 1\n      end, names)\n    end\n    if line:match(\"^%S+%s+follow%s+%S*$\") then\n      return vim.tbl_filter(function(name)\n        return name:lower():find(arglead:lower(), 1, true) == 1\n      end, require(\"hedgesync\").names(0))\n    end\n    if line:match(\"^%S+%s+url%s+%S*$\") then\n      return vim.tbl_filter(function(name)\n        return name:find(arglead, 1, true) == 1\n      end, { \"edit\", \"publish\", \"slide\" })\n    end\n    return {}\n  end,\n})\n\n-- :e hedgedoc://md.example.com/abc123 (also `nvim hedgedoc://...`, quickfix\n-- entries, jumps)\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufReadCmd\", {\n  pattern = \"hedgedoc://*\",\n  callback = function(ev)\n    local hs = require(\"hedgesync\")\n    if hs.session(ev.buf) then\n      return\n    end\n    local name = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(ev.buf)\n    if name == hs.buf_name(hs.http_url(name)) then\n      -- Read it like a file: load into this buffer and wait for the text, so\n      -- `+42`, quickfix line numbers and marks land where they should.\n      hs.open(name, { buf = ev.buf, wait = 10000 })\n      return\n    end\n    local buf = ev.buf\n    vim.schedule(function()\n      hs.open(name)\n      -- open() created or reused its own buffer; drop the placeholder.\n      if vim.api.nvim_buf_is_valid(buf) and not hs.session(buf) then\n        pcall(vim.api.nvim_buf_delete, buf, { force = true })\n      end\n    end)\n  end,\n})\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"VimLeavePre\", {\n  callback = function()\n    if package.loaded[\"hedgesync\"] then\n      require(\"hedgesync\").close_all(3000)\n    end\n  end,\n})\n",
};
